Hi,

I am making a heatmap and using 3 variables.  They respectively represent: the X-axis, Y-axis and the intensity of the color.  I want to use a 4th to change the color.  Can this be done?

Here's a mock-up of what I have:

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-96Am0oPB3zM/ViZfQDanQNI/AAAAAAAAABA/QUrfCuMqtEs/s1600/mock.jpg>
Days are on the X-axis.  I'd really love to be able to turn the weekend days blue and keep the weekdays green.

Here's the code:
 m_date = c( rep("2015-09-13", 3), rep("2015-09-14", 3), rep("2015-09-15", 3))
 M_date = as.Date(m_date) M_hour = c(11, 12, 13, 11, 12, 13, 11, 12, 13)
 M_Count = c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9)
 M_WE = c(1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
 Mock = data.frame(M_date, M_hour, M_Count, M_WE)
 p1 = qplot(M_date, M_hour, fill=M_Count, data=Mock, geom="tile")
 p1 = p1 + scale_x_date() + scale_y_reverse() + scale_fill_gradient(low = "white", high = "green2")
 print(p1)

I want to set the color using: M_WE.  I was able to create new columns for weekend and weekday counts, and two separate graphs but then was not able to combine them.

Thanks in Advance,
Dustin

