MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

For the first time, I got an error when reading data from dput(), but I figured out that the problem was that you made month (mes) a factor and tried to construct lines across its levels. It can be done, but you need to set a group aesthetic on device.category in order to get it. I scaled down your data and chose to plot it with respect to a created date variable, whereby I could manufacture a custom axis label for the date. Pardon my non-Unicode naming scheme :)

d3 <- data.frame(ano = rep(c(2014, 2015), times = c(12, 27)),
         mes = c(7L, 7L, 8L, 9L, 9L, 10L, 10L, 10L, 11L,

     11L, 12L, 12L, 1L, 1L, 2L, 2L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 4L, 4L, 4L, 5L,
     5L, 6L, 6L, 6L, 7L, 7L, 7L, 8L, 8L, 8L, 9L, 9L, 9L, 10L,
     10L, 10L),

         device.category = factor(c(1L, 2L, 1L, 1L,

     2L, 1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 1L, 2L, 1L, 2L, 1L, 2L, 3L,
     1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 3L, 1L,

     2L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 3L), levels = 1L:3L, labels = c("desktop", "mobile",
     "tablet")),

         sesiones = c(58L, 1L, 7L, 33L, 3L,
     47L, 4L, 2L, 11L, 2L, 47L, 2L, 48L, 2L, 18L, 4L, 248L, 7L,
     2L, 309L, 7L, 1L, 543L, 7L, 100L, 18L, 2L, 138L, 30L, 2L,
     118L, 35L, 3L, 135L, 46L, 3L, 89L, 49L, 2L))

d3$date <- as.Date(with(d3, paste(ano, mes, "01", sep = "-")))

library(ggplot2)
library(scales)
ggplot(d3, aes(x = date, y = sesiones, color = device.category)) +
     theme_bw() +
     geom_point() + geom_line(size = 1) +
     scale_x_date(labels = date_format("%b\n%Y")) +
     theme(legend.position = c(1, 1),
           legend.justification = c("right", "top"))

I put the legend inside the plot region in order to provide more room for the graph. If you just want the month names, change the argument of date_format() to "%b". To get every month labeled (without year), try

ggplot(d3, aes(x = date, y = sesiones, color = device.category)) +
     theme_bw() +
     geom_point() + geom_line(size = 1) +
     scale_x_date(breaks = seq(as.Date("2014-07-01"), as.Date("2015-10-01"),
                               by = "month"),
                  labels = date_format("%b")) +
     theme(legend.position = c(1, 1),
           legend.justification = c("right", "top"))

As for your original attempts, there are some problems:

1. Since you defined mes as an (ordered) factor, geom_line() will not work by itself since it requires a numeric x-variable. When given a factor, it silently ignores the call. You need to set a group = aesthetic before geom_line() will work. But...
2. You have repeat values of certain months over 2014 and 2015, so the plot that would get rendered is probably not what you would have expected, which is why I surmise you resorted to faceting by year.

Converting to Date format and specializing the date labels seems to be a reasonable compromise under the assumption that you really wanted a time plot. If instead you really wanted a month plot separated by year per product category, here's an alternative:

# Convert month and year to factor
d3$mes2 <- factor(d3$mes, levels = 1:12, labels = month.abb)
d3$ano2 <- factor(d3$ano)

ggplot(d3, aes(x = mes2, y = sesiones, group = ano2, color = ano2)) +
    theme_bw() +
    geom_point() + geom_line(size = 1) +
    facet_wrap(~ device.category, ncol = 1, scales = "free_y") +
    labs(x = "mes", color = "ano")

HTH,
Dennis

